<title>UK: Shell promotes Cox, de Krij resigns.</title>
<headline>Shell promotes Cox, de Krij resigns.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Dutch oil major Royal Dutch/Shell said on Monday that its deputy group treasurer Rupert Cox would become group controller from March 13.</p>
<p>He succeds Jan de Kreij, who has resigned from the group, it said in a statement. It gaving no motive for the resignation.</p>
<p>Cox, who has been with Shell for over 30 years, will also become a director of Shell International Ltd.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
